<com:TContent ID="body">

<h1>TInlineFrame Samples</h1>

<table class="sampletable">

<tr><td class="samplenote">
An inline frame with default settings, loading another page of this tutorial:
</td><td class="sampleaction">
<com:TInlineFrame FrameUrl="?page=GettingStarted.AboutPrado" />
</td></tr>

<tr><td class="samplenote">
Sized with <tt>Width</tt> and <tt>Height</tt>, and labeled for assistive technology:
</td><td class="sampleaction">
<com:TInlineFrame
	FrameUrl="?page=GettingStarted.AboutPrado"
	Width="500"
	Height="200"
	Attributes.title="About PRADO" />
</td></tr>

<tr><td class="samplenote">
Styled with CSS instead of the deprecated presentational properties. The border and the
spacing come from the <tt>Style</tt> property:
</td><td class="sampleaction">
<com:TInlineFrame
	FrameUrl="?page=GettingStarted.AboutPrado"
	Width="500"
	Height="200"
	Style="border:2px solid #4a7ebb; margin:8px; float:right"
	Attributes.title="About PRADO" />
</td></tr>

<tr><td class="samplenote">
The deprecated properties still render. This frame sets <tt>Align</tt>,
<tt>MarginWidth</tt>, <tt>MarginHeight</tt>, <tt>ScrollBars</tt>, and
<tt>ShowBorder</tt>, which write HTML attributes that HTML5 dropped. A browser may ignore
any of them:
</td><td class="sampleaction">
<com:TInlineFrame
	FrameUrl="?page=GettingStarted.AboutPrado"
	Width="500"
	Height="200"
	MarginWidth="20"
	MarginHeight="20"
	Align="Right"
	ScrollBars="None"
	ShowBorder="false" />
</td></tr>

</table>

</com:TContent>
